{title: Work, for the Night Is Coming}
{artist: Annie L. Walker / Lowell Mason}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: D}
{key_original: F}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Work, for the night is coming, work through the morning hours
[A7]Work while the dew is sparkling, work 'mid springing [D]flowers
Work when the day grows brighter, [G]work in the glowing [D]sun
Work, for the [A7]night is coming, when [D]man's work is done
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Work, for the night is coming, work through the sunny noon
[A7]Fill brightest hours with labor, rest comes sure and [D]soon
Give every flying minute [G]something to keep in [D]store
Work, for the [A7]night is coming, when [D]man works no more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Work, for the night is coming, under the sunset skies
[A7]While their bright tints are glowing, work, for daylight [D]flies
Work till the last beam fadeth, [G]fadeth to shine no [D]more
Work, while the [A7]night is darkening, when [D]man's work is o'er
{end_of_verse}
